1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,163
FoodLink turns one browser tab into a food rescue dispatch desk.

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:13,257
Every lot, route and household is simulated offline in plain JavaScript, with no accounts and no network calls.

3
00:00:13,878 --> 00:00:19,002
The dispatch map routes the volunteer van through donors and pantries.

4
00:00:19,172 --> 00:00:26,976
Each stop badge stays glued to its node, and every label picks a clear spot, so the route never overlaps itself.

5
00:00:27,596 --> 00:00:31,359
The Dispatch outcome ledger reads off the same plan.

6
00:00:31,529 --> 00:00:41,253
This farmers market run rescues one hundred eighty three kilograms and four hundred sixty four servings, with nothing lost to spoilage.

7
00:00:41,423 --> 00:00:53,628
Landfill emissions avoided read one hundred eight point nine kilograms, at the EPA WARM version fifteen low end factor of zero point five nine five per kilogram delivered.

8
00:00:53,799 --> 00:01:01,444
Tightest cold chain margin, route kilometers, minutes and the exact solver all recompute on every control.

9
00:01:02,063 --> 00:01:07,233
Shelf life triage counts every lot down with a Q ten thermal decay model.

10
00:01:07,403 --> 00:01:16,288
Each row reads spoils in minutes at the current ambient temperature, capped by the four hour danger zone clock for T C S foods.

11
00:01:16,458 --> 00:01:23,225
Warm the slider and the urgency tiers flip in place, while the spoils in bar keeps its own color.

12
00:01:23,844 --> 00:01:27,774
The household allocator packs balanced pantry boxes.

13
00:01:27,944 --> 00:01:38,947
Produce, protein, grain and dairy fill against each family's size, while gluten free, nut free, halal, vegetarian and diabetic rules stay hard constraints.

14
00:01:39,118 --> 00:01:44,367
Unmet groups are named on every card, and leftovers are counted honestly.

15
00:01:44,987 --> 00:01:53,395
Four civic scenarios ship in the bench, from a farmers market to a school cafeteria, a storm outage and a holiday surge.

16
00:01:53,565 --> 00:02:01,094
Picking the storm run rewires donors, windows, vehicles and households, and the route replans on the spot.

17
00:02:01,714 --> 00:02:05,158
The whole interface flips to Spanish in one tap.

18
00:02:05,328 --> 00:02:15,051
The manifest tab prints the dispatch sheet and a donation safety checklist, and the data tab exports the scenario as JSON or a share link.

19
00:02:15,671 --> 00:02:20,760
Twenty nine invariants run live in the page from the self tests button.

20
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:29,894
Eight hundred forty five Node tests guard the engines, re verified live inside this recording run with zero honesty findings.

21
00:02:30,065 --> 00:02:33,549
FoodLink. Plan the rescue before the clock does.
